131:15. immediate_decision_informed: Re-entry admissibility boundary: after the engine-runtime repair (rebind to 234ac3524), a further `override recover-blocked` gate (Run Authority grant + custody lease + WBC attempt, action_boundary repair) is required to move blocked→gated so finalize may re-run; the gate itself does not and cannot clear the open circuit. Once admitted, the ordinary finalize re-entry owns the outcome: admission success clears meta.planner_repair (finalize.py:2372); a rejection with the same fingerprint 382e25a2… increments occurrences to 3 and stays blocked (re-block, no auto-loop); a rejection with a different fingerprint resets occurrences to 1 and closes the circuit. The runner being dead means no re-entry is in flight — recovery action (gate) must be externally driven.
